{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Structures","lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic"],"declarations":51,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.kernel_condition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.kernel_condition","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L429-L436","doc":"The transport equation implies `Ĥ_q − π_V ∇ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport.transport_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport.transport_eq","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L427-L427","doc":"**Transport equation**: `π_V(∇ψ) = Ĥ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport.hamiltonian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport.hamiltonian","kind":"def","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L425-L425","doc":"The q-Hamiltonian `Ĥ_q` (LaTeX `\\hat{H}_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport.proj_V_nabla","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport.proj_V_nabla","kind":"def","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L423-L423","doc":"The vertical projection of the covariant derivative `π_V(∇ψ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport.instanton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport.instanton","kind":"def","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L421-L421","doc":"The instanton connection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport.jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport.jet","kind":"def","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L419-L419","doc":"The categorical jet data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport.mk","kind":"ctor","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L415-L415","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransport","kind":"structure","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L410-L427","doc":"**Categorical transport equation**: `ℏ_q π_V(∇ψ) = Ĥ_q(ψ)`.\n(In LaTeX: `\\hat{H}_q`; distinct from the q-shuffle Hopf algebra\n`\\mathcal{H}_q` of Ch 2 and the hook-length product `H_q(λ)` of\nthe knot chapter.)\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-transport}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:glossary-categorical-transport","label":"rem:glossary-categorical-transport","md":"quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-categorical-transport.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_jet_prolongation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_jet_prolongation","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L403-L408","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-jet-prolongation","label":"prop:categorical-jet-prolongation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/categorical-jet-prolongation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.commutes","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L401-L401","doc":"**Prolongation compatibility**: `j¹ ≫ ∇ = ∇' ≫ j¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.connection","kind":"def","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L399-L399","doc":"The original connection `∇ : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.prolonged_connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.prolonged_connection","kind":"def","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L397-L397","doc":"The prolonged connection `∇' : J¹(A) → J¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L392-L392","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJetProlongation","kind":"structure","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L390-L401","doc":"**Proposition (Jet prolongation).**\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:categorical-jet-prolongation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.kernelIncl_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.kernelIncl_exact","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L383-L388","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet.exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet.exact","kind":"theorem","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L381-L381","doc":"**Exactness**: `kernelIncl ≫ jetEval = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet.kernelIncl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet.kernelIncl","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L379-L379","doc":"The kernel inclusion `A ⊗ Ω¹(A) ↪ J¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet.jetEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet.jetEval","kind":"def","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L377-L377","doc":"Jet evaluation `j¹ : J¹(A) → A` (the counit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet.jetObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet.jetObj","kind":"def","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L375-L375","doc":"The jet object `J¹(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L373-L373","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet.mk","kind":"ctor","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L369-L369","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalJet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalJet","kind":"structure","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L367-L381","doc":"**Categorical jet object**: `J¹(A) = A ⊗_C Ω¹(A)`.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-jet}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-jet","label":"def:categorical-jet","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-jet.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_dq_squared_nonvanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_dq_squared_nonvanishing","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L345-L365","doc":"**`d_q²` non-vanishing** (per-instance form) — **this restates its own\nhypothesis.**\n\nThe conclusion is the class field `nonvanishing` verbatim, so the\ndeclaration derives nothing.  That is deliberate rather than an oversight:\nas the removal note above records, *whether* `hq` / `hd_sq` / `hcross`\nimply the non-vanishing is the open question, and until it is answered no\ninstance should be derivable from the conclusion.  The carrier is\nparametrised on `(cqd, hq, hd_sq, hcross)` and is honestly uninhabited.\nDisclosure added 2026-09-05 per bean `qou-pqmw`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasDqSquaredNonvanishing.nonvanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasDqSquaredNonvanishing.nonvanishing","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L322-L322","doc":"The non-vanishing conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasDqSquaredNonvanishing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasDqSquaredNonvanishing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L313-L313","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasDqSquaredNonvanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasDqSquaredNonvanishing","kind":"class","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L308-L322","doc":"**`d_q²` non-vanishing — typeclass.**\nPer-instance witness that the `q`-deformed curvature is\nnon-zero for a specific `(C, cqd)` choice with the\nclassical-vanishing and cross-term hypotheses already in\nscope. Replaces the universal axiom over all monoidal `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_dq_squared_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_dq_squared_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L260-L276","doc":"**Classical limit of d_q².**\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:categorical-dq-squared}`\n\nWhen `q = 1`, `d_q²` vanishes whenever the classical `d²` vanishes.\nThis is the classical-limit direction; for the non-vanishing direction\n(`d_q² ≠ 0` when `q ≠ 1`) see `categorical_dq_squared_nonvanishing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_self_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_self_duality","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L229-L258","doc":"**Proposition (Categorical self-duality).**\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:categorical-self-duality}`\n\nAny `CategoricalInstanton` is self-dual by construction: self-duality\nis encoded as the `self_dual` field of the structure.  This is a\nstructural accessor theorem and derives nothing.\n\nThe pointer this docstring carried until 2026-09-07 — \"for the\nderivation of self-duality from the variational principle see\n`variational_einstein`\" — went to the wrong place.\n`QOU.variational_einstein` states `ca.gravity = einsteinTensor +\nstressTensor`, the Einstein equation, and is itself a projection of\n`HasCategoricalEOM.einstein`; `variational_yang_mills` states the\ngauge equation of motion.  Neither is the self-duality step.\n\nThe derivation the block claims — that every critical point of the\ncategorical Yang-Mills functional is an instanton — is the Bogomolny\ndecomposition, and it lives in the manuscript proof\n`prf:categorical-self-duality`, not in Lean.  Formalising it needs the\ndagger-category decomposition `∫(F* · F) = 2∫(F⁻* · F⁻) + ∫(F ∧_q F)`\nand the topological invariance of the second term; the structure here\ncarries no variational data at all, so the implication cannot be\nstated against it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-self-duality","label":"prop:categorical-self-duality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-self-duality.md"},{"@id":"block:prf:categorical-self-duality","label":"prf:categorical-self-duality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-self-duality-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_irreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_irreducible","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L210-L227","doc":"**Categorical irreducibility** (per-instance form,\n[`lem:categorical-irreducible`]).\n\nIn a quantum observable universe, the adjoint-rep hom-space vanishes:\n`Hom(𝟙, Ad(A))` is a subsingleton.  Derived from the two hypotheses of\n`HasCategoricalIrreducibility` — trace-freeness of `Ad(A)` and\nnon-degeneracy of `∫_A` — by cancelling the monomorphism, which is the\nmanuscript proof of `prf:categorical-irreducible`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:categorical-irreducible","label":"prf:categorical-irreducible","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-irreducible-proof.md"},{"@id":"block:lem:categorical-irreducible","label":"lem:categorical-irreducible","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-irreducible.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility.form_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility.form_mono","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L162-L162","doc":"**Non-degeneracy of `∫_A` (observability axiom).** The restricted\nform `ι ≫ ∫_A` is a monomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility.form_indistinguishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility.form_indistinguishes","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L156-L156","doc":"**Trace-freeness of `Ad(A)`.** `Ad(A)` is the trace-free part of\n`A ⊗ A^∨`, so the Frobenius form `∫_A` restricted along `ι` does not\ndistinguish morphisms out of the unit: `∫_A ∘ ι ∘ s = ∫_A ∘ ι ∘ t`\nfor all `s, t : 𝟙 → Ad(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility.mk","kind":"ctor","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalIrreducibility","kind":"class","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L124-L162","doc":"**Categorical irreducibility — hypotheses of the manuscript proof.**\n\nCarries the two *inputs* of the argument in\n[`prf:categorical-irreducible`], parameterised by the inclusion\n`ι : Ad(A) ↪ A` of the adjoint object (`A` is self-dual, so\n`A ⊗ A^∨ ≃ A ⊗ A`; `ι` is the trace-free part sitting inside it):\n\n* **trace-freeness** — `∫_A` vanishes on `Ad(A)`, so it cannot\n  separate two morphisms `𝟙 → Ad(A)`;\n* **non-degeneracy** — the observability axiom, stated as\n  `Mono (ι ≫ ∫_A)`.\n\nNeither field is the conclusion `Subsingleton (𝟙 ⟶ Ad(A))`; the\nconclusion is *derived* from them in `categorical_irreducible` by\ncancelling the mono. They are of course jointly **equivalent** to it —\nthat is what it means for the manuscript proof to be correct — but the\nequivalence runs through the cancellation step, which is the argument.\nCompare the field this class used to carry, which *was* the conclusion\nverbatim (see the removal note below).\n\nStated in zero-free form (`s ≫ f = t ≫ f` rather than `s ≫ f = 0`)\nbecause `C` is not assumed to have zero morphisms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalInstanton.self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalInstanton.self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L101-L101","doc":"**Self-duality**: `⋆_q(F_∇) = F_∇`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalInstanton.hodge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalInstanton.hodge","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The q-Hodge star involution on `Ω²(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalInstanton.curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalInstanton.curvature","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L97-L97","doc":"The curvature `F_∇ = ∇² : A → Ω²(A)` (represented as endo). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalInstanton.connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalInstanton.connection","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The connection morphism `∇ : A → A ⊗ Ω¹(A)` (represented as endo). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalInstanton.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalInstanton.mk","kind":"ctor","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalInstanton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalInstanton","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L87-L101","doc":"**Categorical instanton**: a connection whose curvature is self-dual\nwith respect to the q-Hodge star `⋆_q`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-instanton}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-instanton","label":"def:categorical-instanton","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-instanton.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq_classical","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L72-L85","doc":"When `q = 1`, `d_q` reduces to `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.dq","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L64-L70","doc":"The q-deformed derivative `d_q` as a morphism: `q⁻¹ d + (1 − q⁻¹) π_V ≫ d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.proj_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.proj_H","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L57-L62","doc":"The horizontal projection `π_H = id − π_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V_idem","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Idempotency of the vertical projection: `π_V ∘ π_V = π_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q_mul_qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q_mul_qinv","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L53-L53","doc":"`qinv` is the inverse of `q`. Replaces the former `q_ne_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.qinv","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L51-L51","doc":"A two-sided inverse for `q`, carried as **data**.\n\n`R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is a ring, not a field: it has no `Inv` instance, so\n`q⁻¹` cannot be *written* even though the indeterminate is invertible in\nit. Carrying the inverse explicitly, with its defining relation below, is\n**strictly stronger** than the `q_ne_zero` it replaces — over a ring,\ninvertible is not implied by nonzero. And the block needs the stronger\nform: `d_q = q⁻¹ d + (1 − q⁻¹) π_V ∘ d` requires `q⁻¹` to *exist*, which\n`q ≠ 0` does not give. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.q","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`, over the formal ground ring.\n\nWas `q : ℝ`. `def:substrate-parameter` puts the deformation parameter in\n`End(𝟙) ≅ R_q`, not in `ℝ`, and the co-located sibling had already made\nthe move (bean `qou-u87j`); this copy is the one that had not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.proj_V","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The vertical projection `π_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.d_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.d_classical","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The classical differential `d : Ωᵏ(A) → Ωᵏ⁺¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L31-L31","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.mk","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Instanton.lean#L21-L55","doc":"**Categorical q-deformed exterior derivative**.\n\nOn a quantum observable universe with weight decomposition `π_H, π_V`\nand substrate parameter `q`, the q-deformed exterior derivative is\n`d_q = q⁻¹ d + (1 − q⁻¹) π_V ∘ d`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-q-ext-deriv}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-q-ext-deriv","label":"def:categorical-q-ext-deriv","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}